WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.739
You've built your first Managed App,

00:00:02.749 --> 00:00:06.570
maybe just by describing it to the App skill in Copilot Cowork.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.650
Here's what happened behind the scenes.

00:00:09.613 --> 00:00:18.935
Wherever you build, whether in Cowork, Copilot Studio, Copilot Code, VS Code, the GitHub Copilot app, or tools like Claude and Lovable,

00:00:18.945 --> 00:00:26.203
the source lands in a Git repository Microsoft manages, and the app runs on the Copilot Managed Runtime.

00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:29.636
Your app was also pinned to an environment.

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:33.576
Built in Cowork, that's your personal developer environment.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.940
And that environment does a lot of work for you:

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.154
security controls, governance policies, monitoring, inventory,

00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:44.040
deployment pipelines and lifecycle management.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.420
Every app gets all of it, from the very first one.

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:50.203
Each environment belongs to a group.

00:00:50.853 --> 00:00:55.179
Admins define the rules once, for the whole group, and every environment in it,

00:00:55.189 --> 00:00:58.263
and every app pinned there, follows them automatically.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.399
That's a big difference from other vibe-coding and low-code tools,

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:05.050
where governance is scattered across separate admin consoles.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:10.229
Here, it's managed centrally in the Microsoft 365 admin center,

00:01:10.239 --> 00:01:15.090
with advanced controls in the Power Platform admin center.
